A||||9||BENGAL4||harmonic balancer
Z||000000||BENGAL4||07-16-99||04:59 PM||||I am installing a timing set on my 86 GT. I have never used a puller before so I am not sure that I am doing it correctly. Do I use the bolts supplied with the puller or use the ones from my pulley? I keep turning and turning the main bolt but I dont seem to get anywhere. Are the balancers that hard to remove? Please help.  
Z||000001||PaUL||07-16-99||05:25 PM||||Dont use a claw type puller, it will damage the balancer. The one you are supposed to use is the flat kind that looks like a "Y". If none of the bolts that came with the puller have the same threads as the balancer, use the ones that held the pulley on. Remove the main large center bolt completely first. Cover the bolt hole with a socket to protect the threads. The puller will pull the balancer off the crank while pushing against it.
Z||000002||JetroGT||07-16-99||08:42 PM||||When you remove the center bolt you will need a good impact wrench. I tried it with a simple hammer impact and it did not budge.
Z||000003||PaUL||07-16-99||08:57 PM||||thats because you are weak like a girl.....just kidding, but I got my off with a breaker bar.
Z||000004||BENGAL4||07-16-99||10:13 PM||||Thanks for the quick responses. The puller I have is indeed a Y type. The bolts supplied with the puller are the right threads but they are long. Now correct me but when you say remove the main bolt do you mean turning it clockwise as to push into the hub? That is what I was doing buyt it looked like I was not lined up right because after numerous turns, it looked uneven. If you guys could explain exactly how to connect it to the balancer and how it pulls or pushes it off of the hub I think I could do it. I am not mechanicaly challenged and a ay trt
Z||000005||BENGAL4||07-16-99||10:16 PM||||I hit the wrong button. Now as I was saying, I am not a bad mechanic but for some reason this is puzzling me. <br> <p>
Z||000006||batboy||07-17-99||12:05 AM||||I'm assuming you did remove the large bolt in the center of the balancer first, right? If set up correctly, that puller will work very slick. The balancer should come right off. The threads on the puller aren't stripped or anything, are they?
Z||000007||BENGAL4||07-17-99||05:15 PM||||Batboy, No the threads are not stripped. Just explain the setup and which bolts to use. The one with the kit are the right thread pattern but are long. If I use the ones from my pulley, it places the puller right next to the balancer. Now one side of the puller is raised and the other is flat. I placed the flat side against the balancer. Just walk me through and maybe I can get this thing off. 
Z||000008||BENGAL4||07-19-99||10:05 PM||||Success. It seems that the puller Autozone lent me was stripped. I went to a rental place and got a different one, put it on and had the balancer off in a few minutes. I guess you have to be smarter than the puller. Thanks everyone for the help.
Z||000009||batboy||07-19-99||10:21 PM||||Oh boy, I finally gave someone a correct answer.
